cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  PumpWatch: a two-tier irrigation pump fault monitoring system with
  leakage-aware evaluation
message: >-
  If you use this software or its evaluation protocol, please cite it using
  the metadata in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Akshaj
    family-names: Shandilya
    email: shandilya.akshaj@gmail.com
repository-code: 'https://github.com/AKSHAJ-SHELL/pumpwatch'
abstract: >-
  A two-tier condition-monitoring architecture for centrifugal pumps: battery
  powered MCU nodes run continuous statistical gating and a local dry-run trip,
  while a shared gateway classifies escalated events with a prior-fitted tabular
  foundation model, so commissioning a new pump substitutes an in-context
  reference set rather than retraining. Includes a five-rung leakage ladder for
  evaluating machinery fault diagnosis under increasingly strict splits, up to
  leave-one-machine-out on eleven in-service pumps.
keywords:
  - condition monitoring
  - fault diagnosis
  - centrifugal pumps
  - data leakage
  - evaluation protocol
  - tabular foundation models
  - in-context learning
  - edge computing
license: MIT
